<para class="os-raise-text-bold">Example 2</para>
<para>A company decides to donate $50,000 to charity. It will select up to 20 charitable organizations, as nominated by its employees. Each selected organization will receive an equal donation amount.
</para>
<para>What is the relationship between the number of students, \(s\), and the dollar amount each student will receive,
  \(d\)?<br/>
  To begin, let's examine some specific values to help uncover the pattern.
</para>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="b2836c0e-a2fe-472a-abf6-e625fc5bbc55" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="0" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--Q5-->
  <exercise data-content-id="c139ee28-73dc-4737-9b32-167f1010a9aa" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="10000">
    <problem>
      <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="5" type="enumerated">
        <item>If 5 organizations are selected, how much will each charity receive?</item>
      </list>
      <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! $10,000</para>
    </solution>
        </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q6-->
  <exercise data-content-id="b994dfe2-48dc-40bb-afa4-4e2b4b067038" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="5000">
